    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38019" root="لهب" body-key="l">
    
      8 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">التهبت النَّارُ</span></b> , quasi-pass. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَلْهَبَ</span>, (K,) <i>The
fire flamed,</i> or <i>blazed:</i> (S:) or <i>flamed,</i> or <i>blazed,
free from smoke.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">التهب عَلَيْهِ</span> (tropical:)  <i>He was
incensed,</i> or <i>inflamed with anger, against him.</i>
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">التهب</span> and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تلهّب</span></b>  [<i>It</i> (any part of the
body) <i>became inflamed</i>]. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  See 5.

